prompt:
Zelda-style original in-game screenshot recreation
Art style: Nintendo Switch Breath of the Wild / Tears of the Kingdom in-game screenshot style; no cinematic CG, no photorealistic photography, no HDR realistic lighting, no wet-looking realistic materials; no title screen, no Nintendo or Zelda logo, no trademark page, no watermark
{argument name="game_version" default="TOTK (Tears of the Kingdom) default outfit"}, {argument name="party" default="Link + Zelda traveling together"}

Hyrule map region: {argument name="location" default="Beijing · Forbidden City"}
Scene elements: {argument name="scene_elements" default="Hall of Supreme Harmony roofline, red walls and golden tiles, white marble steps, palace-gate axis, distant corner towers"}
Gameplay moment: {argument name="gameplay_moment" default="Link and Zelda are crossing the plaza in front of the Hall of Supreme Harmony, investigating an ancient shrine entrance set into the shadow of the palace wall; no stamina is consumed and the stamina wheel is not shown"}

Zelda elements: {argument name="zelda_elements" default="TOTK Zonai shrine, classic treasure chest, Sheikah researcher, Bokoblin patrol camp, cooking pot, distant sky monster"}
Location UI text (area-discovery banner): top 「发现！」 (“Discovered!”) / middle 「{argument name="main_place_name" default="北京·故宫"}」 / bottom 「{argument name="parent_place_name" default="北京·东城区"}」; presented in the classic three-line area-discovery layout, with the parent region right-aligned at the bottom, a short dash to the left of the text only, soft glow, no rectangular border, no dark background fill
HUD: appears the way it naturally would in an original BOTW/TOTK screenshot, not cluttered; keep only 1-3 of: minimap, heart/HP meter, interaction prompt, or quest marker
Text: all readable UI text is in Chinese, action verbs are Chinese-only, e.g. 「调查」「打开」「拾取」「烹饪」 (Investigate / Open / Pick Up / Cook)

Scene requirements: the architectural silhouette and landmark features of the real-world location must be clearly recognizable; modern-day tourists, staff, ticket gates, ticket signage, plastic barriers, QR codes, and tourism signage should all be reimagined as Hyrule villagers, stable keepers, traveling merchants, Sheikah researchers, wooden signs, shrine mechanisms, or horse-cart props; the image should look like a player is actively exploring with their character, not a travel poster, movie still, cover key visual, or modern app screenshot.

Negative prompt: no photorealistic travel photo, no cinematic CG, no official logo, no watermark, no modern tourists, no modern uniforms, no QR code, no English UI words, no garbled glyphs, no fake app interface, no overcrowded HUD, no title screen, no poster typography, no signature.
